      "claim": "Among visible contexts with direct human F measurements, saccharin (a small sulfonamide-containing molecule) had absolute oral F of 0.80–0.88 by AUC and urinary excretion in both fed and fasted states, well above the 20% threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C07", "C18", "C26", "C27"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 context records consistently show high oral F in their respective contexts (nifedipine ~90% in cirrhotic patients, pethidine 0.83–0.87 in cirrhotic patients, tolfenamic acid ~100–113% in cirrhotic patients, 2,4-D virtually 100% in rats), providing no affirmative low-F evidence for the query.",
